                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L%C3%B6b%27s+axiom"} Löb's axiom
          %h2#references References
          %p The terminology “S4” in modal logic originates with:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clarence+I.+Lewis"}> Clarence I. Lewis
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cooper+H.+Langford"} Cooper H. Langford
              %em Symbolic Logic
              (1932), Dover (2000) &amp;lbrack;App. II
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.hist-analytic.com/Lewisstrict.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/possible+worlds"}> possible worlds
            ”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kripke+semantics"} Kripke semantics
            of S4 originates with:
          %ul
            %li#Kripke63
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+A.+Kripke"}> Saul A. Kripke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Semantical Analysis of Modal Logic I. Normal Modal Propositional Calculi
              %strong 9
              5-6 (1963) 67-96 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/malq.19630090502"}> doi:10.1002/malq.19630090502
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Kripke80
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+Kripke"}> Saul Kripke
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Naming+and+Necessity"} Naming and Necessity
              (1980)
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} natural deduction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+operator"} modal operator
            as a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
          %ul
            %li#BiermanDePaiva96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gavin+M.+Bierman"}> Gavin M. Bierman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"} Valeria de Paiva
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Intuitionistic necessity revisited
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2810611_Intuitionistic_Necessity_Revisited"} researchgate
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Bierman-dePaiva-NecessityRevisited.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gavin+M.+Bierman"}> Gavin M. Bierman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"} Valeria de Paiva
                %em On an Intuitionistic Modal Logic
                Studia Logica
                %strong 65
                (2000) 383–416 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1005291931660"}> doi:10.1023/A:1005291931660
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Valeria-De-Paiva/publication/226515897_On_An_Intuitionistic_Modal_Logic/links/00b4951ed416906ccc000000/On-An-Intuitionistic-Modal-Logic.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Kobayashi97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Satoshi+Kobayashi"}> Satoshi Kobayashi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monad as modality
                %strong 175
                1 (1997) 29-74 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-3975(96)00169-7"}> doi:10.1016/S0304-3975(96)00169-7
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Natasha Alechina, Michael Mendler,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"} Valeria de Paiva
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical and Kripke Semantics for Constructive S4 Modal Logic
                %em Computer Science Logic. CSL 2001
                Lecture Notes in Computer Science
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 2142
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-44802-0_21"} doi:10.1007/3-540-44802-0_21
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Simpson"}> Alex Simpson
              ,
              %em The proof theory and semantics of intuitionistic modal logic
              (1994) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://era.ed.ac.uk/handle/1842/407"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/1842/407"} handle:1842/407
          %p
            More on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mn 5
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S5_{(m)}
            and their applications in Artificial Intelligence can be found in
          %ul
            %li
              J.- J. Ch. Meyer and W. Van der Hoek,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Epistemic logic for AI and Computer Science
          %p General books on modal logics which treat these logics thoroughly in the general context include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Blackburn"}> Patrick Blackburn
